##### copilot plugin
Usage: copilot plugin <COMMAND>

Manage plugins and plugin marketplaces.

Plugins extend Copilot CLI with additional skills, agents, hooks, MCP servers,
and LSP servers. They can be installed from plugin marketplaces, GitHub
repositories, repository subdirectories, or direct git URLs.

One marketplace is included by default:
  awesome-copilot   github/awesome-copilot

Use `copilot plugin marketplace browse <name>` to discover available plugins,
or install directly from any GitHub repository.

For more information, see:
https://docs.github.com/copilot/concepts/agents/copilot-cli/about-cli-plugins

Commands:
  install      Install a plugin
  uninstall    Uninstall a plugin
  update       Update a plugin
  list         List installed and --plugin-dir plugins
  enable       Enable a plugin
  disable      Disable a plugin
  marketplace  Manage plugin marketplaces

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

##### copilot plugin marketplace
Usage: copilot plugin marketplace <COMMAND>

Manage plugin marketplaces.

Marketplaces are GitHub repositories containing a `marketplace.json` file that
indexes available plugins. Add a marketplace to browse and install its plugins.

One marketplace is included by default and does not need to be added:
  awesome-copilot   github/awesome-copilot

For more information, see:
https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/copilot-cli/customize-copilot/plugins-marketplace

Commands:
  add     Add a marketplace
  remove  Remove a marketplace
  list    List registered marketplaces
  browse  Browse plugins in a marketplace
  update  Update marketplace plugin catalogs

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

##### copilot mcp
Usage: copilot mcp <COMMAND>

Manage MCP server configuration.

MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers extend Copilot with additional tools
and capabilities. Servers can be local (stdio) processes or remote (HTTP/SSE)
endpoints.

Configuration is loaded from multiple sources:
  User       ~/.copilot/mcp-config.json
  Workspace  .mcp.json or .github/mcp.json
  Plugin     Installed plugins with MCP servers

Use `copilot mcp list` to see all configured servers,
or `copilot mcp get <name>` for details about a specific server.

Commands:
  list     List configured MCP servers
  get      Show server details
  add      Add an MCP server
  remove   Remove an MCP server
  enable   Enable an MCP server
  disable  Disable an MCP server

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

##### copilot skill
Usage: copilot skill <COMMAND>

Manage skills available to Copilot.

Skills are reusable instructions (SKILL.md files) that extend Copilot with
specialized capabilities. They are discovered from several sources:
  Project   .github/skills/, .agents/skills/, or .claude/skills/
  Personal  ~/.copilot/skills/ or ~/.agents/skills/
  Plugin    Installed plugins that bundle skills
  Custom    Directories added with `copilot skill add <directory>`

Use `copilot skill add` to add a skill from a file, URL, or directory.

Commands:
  list     List available skills
  add      Add a skill from a file, URL, or directory
  remove   Remove a skill or custom skill directory
  enable   Enable a skill
  disable  Disable a skill

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

##### copilot instruction
Usage: copilot instruction <COMMAND>

Inspect the instruction sources a session would load.

Instructions come from your repository, the working directory, your
personal configuration, and installed plugins.

Commands:
  list  List discovered instruction sources

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

##### copilot lsp
Usage: copilot lsp <COMMAND>

Inspect the language servers configured for this CLI.

Starting, stopping, and reloading language servers needs a running
session; use the interactive `/lsp` command for those.

Commands:
  list  List configured language servers

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

##### copilot sandbox
Usage: copilot sandbox <COMMAND>

Manage command sandboxing outside an interactive session.

Use `copilot help sandbox` for how sandboxing works, and the interactive
`/sandbox` command to change its settings.

Commands:
  ca  Manage the credential proxy certificate authority

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
